### Curbside Pickup — HTTP requests
#
# Ready-made requests for the app's control endpoints. In VS Code, install the
# "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client) and click "Send Request" above any
# request. The app must be running (npm run demo).
#
# Every toggle is a plain SQL UPDATE against PostgreSQL (orders) or MySQL
# (vehicles); Drasi observes the change through CDC and re-evaluates the queries.

@host = http://localhost:3000

### Current state (initial snapshot of every stream) + SQL log
GET {{host}}/api/state

### SQL log only
GET {{host}}/api/log

### Toggle order 1 (preparing <-> ready) — PostgreSQL
POST {{host}}/api/orders/1/toggle

### Toggle order 2 (preparing <-> ready) — PostgreSQL
POST {{host}}/api/orders/2/toggle

### Move vehicle A1234 (Parking <-> Curbside) — MySQL
POST {{host}}/api/vehicles/A1234/toggle

### Move vehicle B5678 (Parking <-> Curbside) — MySQL
POST {{host}}/api/vehicles/B5678/toggle

### Reset everything (all orders preparing, all vehicles Parking)
POST {{host}}/api/reset

### Live event stream (multiplexes every SSE reaction route; Ctrl+C to stop)
GET {{host}}/events
Accept: text/event-stream
